# Append-only runner rollup files are edited independently by every worktree
# (this task's .jdone plus any sibling branch's report) and are merged back into
# manus-parity, which keeps an equivalent file of its own. A normal 3-way merge
# therefore conflicts on nearly every region, which forces a hand-resolve every
# time and repeatedly produced "MERGE CONFLICT with latest manus-parity in:
# .jdone" gate failures. The union driver instead concatenates both sides, which
# is exactly the intended outcome for these files: each report stays intact and
# the result is a superset of both parents.
.jdone merge=union
.jcode-done merge=union
